# TODO - The Simpsons Arcade Game

## Objective

Original Konami arcade four-player World set 1;
preserve original four-player cooperative gameplay and pixel art.

## Acceptance

- Replace the obsolete coin-dependent prototype with free play only.
  No virtual coins, paid continues or classic arcade mode may ship.
- Provide a visible modern main menu, Enter/Start to play immediately,
  character selection, local multiplayer joining, pause, settings and
  exit using shared session/menu/input mechanisms.
- Verify visible characters and enemies and actual keyboard movement,
  controller and touch input; hidden synthetic smoke is supplementary.
- Complete real adaptive widescreen scene extension and responsive HUD
  and touch placement. Keep per-player control settings and defaults.
- Default to one local player with WASD movement, Space jump and left
  mouse button attack. Additional seats join explicitly using independent
  bindings. Support configurable keyboard, mouse, gamepad and touch
  controls, persistent profiles and reset in the shared settings menu.
- Escape is the single keyboard pause/resume control for the local game.
  Remove per-seat keyboard pause requirements. Show join and control
  instructions in the pause/settings menus, not in the gameplay HUD.
  Retain health, lives and essential gameplay status without prompts.
- Admit entering enemies just outside or at the actual visible camera
  edges, including adaptive viewports, rather than visibly popping into
  the interior. Preserve reference spawn conditions and world bounds.
- Remove avoidable black side borders in supported wide scenes by using
  real additional scene content and precise uniform viewport geometry.
  Verify the owner's maximized desktop aspect ratio, resize and fullscreen.
  Physically verify native aspect-fit, integer, fill/crop, stretch and
  adaptive display modes, high-DPI mapping and device remapping.
  Keep safe aspect-fit fallback only where genuine extension is unavailable.
- Verify actual audible playback on the host, not only dummy audio and
  submission counters. Diagnose device selection, gain and queue delivery;
  expose persistent master, effects and music settings where supported.
  Record the selected physical audio device and effective volume.
  Reconstruct the original music and other missing cues separately.

- Use only a selected lawful original edition and locally imported assets.
- Reuse shared engine mechanisms and extend them where necessary.
- Verify observable gameplay or application behaviour, saves and input.
- Report actual Linux, Android and browser acceptance where applicable.
- Run `cargo validate` and record unresolved parity or platform limits.

- Check original input under
  `.reference/games/simpsons-arcade/`.
- If required media is missing, record the blocker in Evidence; recheck
  and clear it when a suitable original edition becomes available.

