Matched original-machine diagonal, left-only, up-only and idle Marge
observations confirm two pixels per tick on each independent component.
The two repeated diagonal runs matched all 576 raw and RGB captures.
Isolated attacks for all four stations retained their opening facing
until recovery, even when Left was subsequently held. Marge accepted a
same-frame direction change on attack admission; a later direction
change did not turn the attack. Jump permitted a later turn and full
horizontal movement. Matched attack-direction observations show slow
horizontal drift and no vertical drift for Marge. The title now retains
attack facing after tick zero, models approximate quarter-pixel horizontal
movement, and resumes normal walking at recovery. Fractional rounding,
vertical drift for the other stations and combat hitboxes remain unverified.
Inline regression tests cover diagonal movement, all four stations' attack
facing and drift, recovery, and turning during jump. This supersedes the
previous provisional attack immobility rule.

Native display settings now select shared scaling and desktop fullscreen
through the local launch catalogue or command-line overrides. The fixed
street preview uses temporary aspect-fit fallback for adaptive mode;
real camera extension with additional imported scene content and responsive
HUD/touch placement is still required. Fill is unavailable with the fixed
touch panel to prevent clipping essential controls.

Local keyboard and controller-button profiles can override each of the
four stations independently. Regression tests route remapped inputs,
reject old bindings and verify the replacement controller receives the
vacant station's profile. A combined hidden title run passed with a
custom profile and integer scaling. Touch and analog remapping,
interactive settings and physical devices remain open.

The optional single touch panel is now selectable for any station, with
per-station button-position profiles. Inline tests verify moved glyphs,
hit regions and station routing. The combined hidden title run passed
with Bart selected, swapped attack/jump and left/right touch positions,
custom keyboard bindings and integer mode. Independent simultaneous
touch panels and hardware testing remain open.

Owner acceptance override: the visible prototype opens onto street art
without an obvious entry prompt; the owner observed a character only
after station Start. The existing coin/Start/continue evidence above
describes historical reference observations and temporary implementation,
